# Ignore rules for `docker build -f backend/Dockerfile .` — BuildKit uses
# `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` when it exists. The context is the repo root,
# which also holds the frontend (node_modules and .next alone are ~36k files)
# and an unrelated project (ClarityLMS); excluding them keeps the context the
# daemon has to pack on every build down to the backend sources.
backend/tests
frontend
ClarityLMS
docs
infra
.config
.migbak
.github
.git
**/bin
**/obj
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/*.log
**/.env*
**/Dockerfile
**/*.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
*.md
*.slnx
package-lock.json
